* LM393 dual voltage comparator, standard 8-pin DIP/SOIC pin order.
* Pin order: 1 OUT1, 2 IN1-, 3 IN1+, 4 GND, 5 IN2+, 6 IN2-, 7 OUT2, 8 VCC.
* Typical classic LM393 model at 5 V: 2 mV input offset, 25 nA input bias,
* 0.8 mA total quiescent current, and approximately 1.3 us response.
* Output is open collector; connect an external pull-up resistor.
* Behavioral model does not model input clamps, output current limiting,
* saturation recovery, temperature corners, or detailed propagation dynamics.
.subckt LM393 OUT1 IN1M IN1P GND IN2P IN2M OUT2 VCC PARAMS: VOS=2m IB=25n TPD=1.3u IQ=0.8m
XCOMP1 OUT1 IN1M IN1P GND VCC LM393_COMP PARAMS: VOS={VOS} IB={IB} TPD={TPD}
XCOMP2 OUT2 IN2M IN2P GND VCC LM393_COMP PARAMS: VOS={VOS} IB={IB} TPD={TPD}
BBIAS VCC GND I={IQ}
.ends LM393

.subckt LM393_COMP OUT INM INP GND VCC PARAMS: VOS=2m IB=25n TPD=1.3u
BIBP GND INP I={IB}
BIBM GND INM I={IB}
BSTATE NRAW GND V={if(V(INP,INM)>VOS,0,V(VCC,GND))}
RDELAY NRAW NCTRL {TPD/(ln(2)*1n)}
CDELAY NCTRL GND 1n
SOUT OUT GND NCTRL GND LM393_SW
.ends LM393_COMP

.model LM393_SW SW(Ron=50 Roff=1G Vt=2.5 Vh=0)
